# scoreboard.tsv — the PERMANENT ledger for {{CAMPAIGN_TITLE}}. One row per experiment.
# RULES: tab-separated; append-only. Never delete or rename a column mid-campaign (it breaks
#   comparability with earlier rows). Keep the PRIMARY column ({{PRIMARY_METRIC_COL}}) position stable.
#   Add campaign-specific columns AFTER the lever columns and BEFORE `notes`; a new column requires the
#   run-writer ({{EVAL_WRITER}}) to emit it. exp_id: 000 = baseline gate, 001 = first method, then 002,003,…;
#   sub-runs 000a/000b; non-config probes prefixed `#`. `verified` = independent-agent verdict (blank
#   until run). `notes` carries "NEW BEST", "CONFIRMS expN", "PROVISIONAL — adapted eval", etc.
# This is the campaign's QUANTITATIVE record (the JOURNAL is narrative). Every experiment's numbers live
#   here: the primary metric, every supplemental metric / sanity score (DIAGNOSTIC columns), and the
#   experiment-type RUN numerics (e.g. epochs trained + best epoch for ML; iterations / wall-clock /
#   n_free_params for fits; seed / n_reps). If a *_COLUMNS group is empty for this campaign, remove it
#   AND its adjacent tab so the header has no blank column.
# COMPARABILITY (the most common silent landmine): `metric_version` / `data_version` tag the FROZEN metric
#   and the dataset/version this row was scored under (e.g. `v1`, `v2_corrected`). A "current best" / ranking
#   claim is valid ONLY WITHIN one (metric_version, data_version) pair — NEVER compare a number across
#   versions. When the metric or data changes, bump the tag and RE-SCORE saved contenders under the new
#   version before comparing; a programmatic check should refuse a cross-version current-best (campaign-status
#   flags it). Every row MUST carry both tags — a blank tag makes the row uncomparable and is a hygiene fail.
# `tier` = the run-length tier from charter.md caps (Scout / Confirmation / Extended; `Baseline` for exp 000).
#   Keep it on EVERY row so scout/confirmation cap-compliance stays machine-auditable — a real campaign lost
#   its tier tag partway through and cap-compliance became unverifiable.
exp_id	timestamp	metric_version	data_version	tier	description	{{LEVER_COLUMNS}}	{{PRIMARY_METRIC_COL}}	{{PRIMARY_SPREAD_COL}}	{{GUARDRAIL_COL}}	{{DIAGNOSTIC_COLUMNS}}	{{RUN_COLUMNS}}	verified	notes
